From ffab7347723d76d8f6680ec73ebde08fb664fe7e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: snarayana <snarayana@student.ethz.ch>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 01:35:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat: raw presharding and a deep-state round-trip check

sharded_state saves `state_dict()` after process_weights_after_loading, MLA
absorption and lazily created aliases have run, and reloads it into a model
whose post-processing already ran on placeholders. Anything a model keeps
outside state_dict, or creates lazily, is lost silently or breaks the load:
sglang#34448 (MXFP4 experts parked on the quant method), sglang#35702 / #19
(attn_mha.kv_b_proj registered on first forward), and GemmaRMSNorm's
non-persistent gemma_weight, derived inside its weight loader.

Raw presharding (`--preshard-format raw`) stores instead, per rank, exactly
the bytes of the original checkpoint that the ordinary load read on that rank,
found by wrapping every tensor the weights iterator yields in a tensor
subclass that records each read as a strided byte box. Serving replays those
bytes through the ordinary load, so every weight loader, post-processing hook
and alias runs as in a default load. Each read is checked against what was
stored (SERVEKIT_RAW_VERIFY, on by default) and the parallel layout is checked
against the one recorded, so a mismatch refuses to serve instead of serving
garbage. Writing is incremental: a tensor's bytes are copied out as soon as
nothing references it, so peak memory is about one 5 GB part.

`servekit.deepstate` fingerprints every tensor a loaded model holds,
including those on quant-method objects, plain attributes and non-persistent
buffers; `SERVEKIT_DEEPSTATE_DIR` dumps them after any load and
`servekit deepstate REF CAND` compares two dumps. It is the generic version of
the quant_guard denylist: a state_dict-only comparison passes on the MXFP4
case, this one does not.

Also: quant_guard now refuses gpt-oss MXFP4 with no --moe-runner-backend for
sharded_state, because sglang resolves auto to triton_kernel below SM100
(arg_groups/model_overrides/gpt_oss.py:106-125 in v0.5.20), and never refuses
a raw preshard.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
